NAME
       mixer - adjust playback volume and pick the audio output

SYNOPSIS
       mixer
       mixer status
       mixer <0-100> | +N | -N
       mixer mute | unmute | toggle
       mixer out <n|auto>
       mixer save | restore

DESCRIPTION
       Controls the mixer of whichever audio driver claimed the card
       (hda or ac97). With no arguments it opens an interactive screen
       showing a volume bar and the list of output devices the codec
       reports.

       On HDA the outputs come from the codec's pin configuration
       defaults, so internal speakers, a headphone jack and a line out
       appear separately. Jacks with presence detection are shown as
       connected or not connected.

KEYS
       left, right  volume down / up in steps of 5
       up, down     move through the output list
       Enter        route playback to the selected output
       m            mute / unmute
       s            save the current settings
       q, Esc       quit

OUTPUT SELECTION
       Selecting Auto lets the driver follow the jacks: a plugged
       headphone wins over the line out, which wins over the internal
       speaker. Selecting a device by name pins playback to it even
       when nothing is plugged in.

FILES
       /etc/audio.conf
              Saved volume, mute state and output. Written by
              "mixer save" (or s in the interactive screen) and applied
              at boot by init.

EXAMPLES
       mixer 60            set the volume to 60%
       mixer -10           turn it down by ten points
       mixer out 1         send playback to output 1
       mixer out auto      go back to following the jacks
